              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_11_image_4.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.546,
            0.177,
            0.792,
            0.323
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.546,
                0.177,
                0.792,
                0.323
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_11_image_5.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.367,
            0.885,
            0.435
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We can estimate the area of any simple closed shape by using a sheet of squared paper or graph paper where every square measures 1 unit × 1 unit or 1 square unit."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.438,
            0.885,
            0.506
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To estimate the area, we can trace the shape onto a piece of transparent paper and place the same on a piece of squared or graph paper and then follow the below conventions—"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.509,
            0.884,
            0.554
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. The area of one full small square of the squared or graph paper is taken as 1 sq unit."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.56,
            0.834,
            0.583
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Ignore portions of the area that are less than half a square."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.589,
            0.884,
            0.612
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. If more than half of a square is in a region, just count it as 1 sq unit."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.616,
            0.864,
            0.649
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. If exactly half the square is counted, take its area as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " sq unit."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.66,
            0.605,
            0.683
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Find the area of the following figures."
            }
          ]
        },
